# Tailwind styling

Style with Tailwind utilities. No `style={{}}`, no new `.css` files, no arbitrary values (`bg-[#fff]`, `px-[13px]`, `text-[var(--sea-ink)]`). Use theme tokens (`bg-background`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`) defined in `src/styles.css`.

Merge classes with `cn()` from `#/lib/utils`. Define variants with `cva`. Never build class names dynamically (`bg-${color}`); the names must appear as complete strings so Tailwind can see them.

Reach for a shadcn primitive before writing a custom one. Add it with:

```bash
pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add button
```

```tsx
// ❌ <div style={{ padding: 13 }} className="bg-[#f6f6f6]" />
// ✅ <div className="bg-muted p-3" />
```
